//? Title: Latent Diffusion: A Frozen Encoder and Unclipped Latent Posterior
//? Subtitle: Native tensor components with editable training and sampling loops
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This report preserves the original latent_diffusion experiment and moves reusable tensor operations into datamunge. Parameter stores, objectives, minibatch loops, optimizer writes and sampling trajectories are visible in the complete program.
)
\toc

> Method, preserved protocol and observed limitations

[Rombach et al., High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models (2021/2022)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.10752) motivates learning diffusion in a frozen representation. This original fixture is much smaller:it uses a 101652-value MNIST VAE with two-coordinate posterior means, rather than a convolutional text-conditioned latent diffusion system. The VAE's selected checkpoint is prepared explicitly below and frozen for all encoding, latent fitting and decoding.

Fitting-only coordinate means/scales standardize the codes. A10-to 32-to 32-to 2 MLP with 1474 values predicts latent noise, with 96 Adam writes in three epochs. The 32-level posterior uses an **unclipped** clean-latent estimate; clipping standardized coordinates would change the model. The program retains full2x2 predictor/transition Jacobians, checkpoint controls, Gaussian-code and VAE-prior comparisons and decoded galleries.

Test epsilon MSE is 0.546270013, versus 1.055734146 for zero prediction and 0.469139333 for a fitting-only full-covariance Gaussian. Raw clean-latent MSE is 581.960276931, exposing terminal-noise sensitivity. Frozen mean-decoding pixel MSE is 0.080653337. These results retain the source's limitations.

> Follow the state through one model operation

The method diagram separates the explicitly supplied state and conditioning from the predictor and the single transition. The caller owns repeated transitions and training.

